  "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255908/assets/b774bc8a08c16c74b78063b7d0b25120dc58cbc6adf18ec469d2e1a3acaca0f8.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $1.25.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=1.25\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$",
